<title>INDIA: Indian soybean firm, oil, meal down.</title>
<headline>Indian soybean firm, oil, meal down.</headline>
<dateline>INDORE, India 1996-10-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Soybean prices were firm on limited availability due to poor arrivals in central Indian markets on Wednesday, dealers said.</p>
<p>After the monsoons, farmers are busy sowing for the winter rabi season. The undertone was strong.</p>
<p>Soyoil prices were down on selling pressure from soyplants and refineries. Demand was poor. Soyoil solvent was down by 100 rupees and soyoil refined was down by 300 rupees per tonne. The undertone was easy.</p>
<p>Soymeal prices were slightly down on slightly lower export demand. Soymeal yellow was $271-272 per tonne in export. Rapeseed extraction was $125 per tonne in export. Rapeseed extraction was 4,300 rupees FOR Bedibunder and was 4,250-4,275 rupees FOR Bhavnagar.</p>
